{
  "description": "BTPS 1.1 document model v2. Each case names a document in documents/ (or gives one inline), optionally changed by `set` (top-level fields replaced), `unset` (top-level fields removed) and `setPath` (each entry sets the value at `path`, an array of keys and indexes: `value` as given, or `repeat` written `times` times followed by `then`, for a file too large to write out). schema: the SDK's parseBtpDocV2 accepts or refuses it. ownership: every entry in a document's references (a credit note's credits, a corrected invoice's correction_of, any other) may only name a document from the envelope's own sender. attachments: the SDK's verifyAttachments accepts or refuses each attachment's file, and names the field at fault (content, size or sha256). payslip: the SDK's reconcilePayslip agrees with the stated results, and reports a disagreement rather than throw. There is no tax-total check: an invoice's and a credit note's line items are a table the protocol does not add up, and a credit note's totalAmount is positive (its type says it is a credit). Every document in documents/ is also checked to be unchanged by parsing, and signed and verified over its JCS form on every runtime.",
  "documentsDir": "documents",
  "keyVector": "kms-signature.vector.json",
  "schema": [
    { "name": "invoice", "document": "invoice.v2.json", "expect": "accept" },
